+## 2026-06-10 (Operational retrospective — 2026.06.370)
+
+- Wrote `results/operational_retro_2026_06_370.json` (schema carnot.operational_retro.v64). The authoritative TIMING DATA block again reported **0 experiment commits since activation** and both RTX 3090s idle (0%). Per the GPU-idle rule this is NOT flagged — there are 0 compute-bound tasks in the block, so `gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null`, locked numerics stay 0/empty, and `estimated_time_savings_pct=0` (no real timing to optimize; no wall-time fabricated).
+- **Headline finding — `detector_gap_suspected=true`, SEVENTH consecutive false zero (.363/.365/.366/.367/.368/.369/.370).** The zero is a known milestone->commit detector artifact, NOT an empty milestone: the on-disk .370 changelog window shows ~11 committed artifacts (range exp3997-exp4007) — the GAP-4 verifier confirmation arms (de-selection coverage, precision confirmation v2, feedback-vs-redraw, harness registration + bit-exact offline replay), the ARC-AGI-3 level-frontier (r11l L4) + FOURTH game first-solve (su15), the ArcMemo solve-transfer v3, hardware continuity, and the capstone exp4007.
+- **Meta-finding:** the prior-milestone "retro commit detector fixed" claim is STILL not verified end-to-end — this .370 retro received another zero timing block, the second subsequent live retro the fix failed to take effect on. Top-3 highest-leverage actions: (1) repair the detector/windowing and prove it end-to-end on .370 (must report exp3997-exp4007, not 0); (2) add a detector-independent glob fallback (results/experiment_*.json since the activation SHA) + a loud self-check that fails when count==0 but artifacts exist; (3) verify-or-revert the prior "detector fixed" claim that has now gone two milestones without taking effect.
+- Appended the .370 narrative to `docs/research-log.md`. No edits to operator-curated docs (roadmap.md, index.html, README.md), research_conductor.py, or research-roadmap.yaml.
